  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "Which of the following numbers has the largest reciprocal?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac13\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac25\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(5\\)",
    "E": "\\(1986\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The reciprocal of a nonzero number is the number that multiplies it to give \\(1\\). The listed numbers have reciprocals\n\\[\n3,\\quad \\frac52,\\quad 1,\\quad \\frac15,\\quad \\frac1{1986},\n\\]\nrespectively. Since \\(5/2<3\\) and the last three reciprocals are at most \\(1\\), the largest reciprocal is \\(3\\). It belongs to \\(\\boxed{\\frac13}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
